Reverse genocide nurses on a no teleport level in a
restricted, lit area. A large, lockable room in the castle
should do nicely. I don't think new monsters will spawn
where you can see them and the nurses can't get away. You
can get around 50 hp per scroll. Do the alchemy trick with
potions of speed, healing, extra healing, gain energy (or
level) and holy water. Each blessed diluted !oFH is worth 8
HP. 200 HP is enough but if it's your first trip, go for
300, but not necessary before Gehennom.
> 
> Any advice?

If you don't have a plan for L's, (m)mf's, R's, ;'s and
green slimes, make one or genocide them. I always carry a
/oFire, /oDig and a /oTeleportation in my inventory, just in
case.

Cast light at every stairway, just in case one gets covered
by an item. You won't want to stop and search on your way
out.

Don't walk around wielding a cockatrice corpse.

Don't pray in Gehennom.

